.","type":"text"}]}]},{"name":"transform","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"An async closure that takes the error from the upstream and returns a new ","type":"text"},{"code":"AsyncSequence","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to be fully consumed for side effects before retrying.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"content":[{"anchor":"return-value","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Return Value"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"An ","type":"text"},{"code":"AsyncSequence","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" that emits the same elements as the upstream but retries on failure using the given strategy,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"performing the transformation before each retry.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"},{"content":[{"anchor":"discussion","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The provided transformation closure is executed "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"before","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" each retry, allowing for side effects such as refreshing tokens or resetting state."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"The closure’s returned "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AsyncSequence"},{"type":"text","text":" is always fully consumed before the retry occurs, but its elements are ignored."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"The element type of the returned sequence does not need to match the upstream’s element type."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This is useful for performing asynchronous side effects like credential refresh before retrying the main sequence."}]},{"anchor":"Example-Refreshing-an-access-token-on-a-401-HTTP-error-before-retrying-the-main-request","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Example: Refreshing an access token on a 401 HTTP error before retrying the main request"},{"type":"codeListing","code":["let mainRequest = URLSession.shared.dataTaskAsyncSequenc